// The other half of bucle_sin_aviso_falso.zy: an iterator the body WRITES.
//
// This is what `ambiguous lifetime` exists to say. The loop advances `i` and
// the body assigns to it as well, so there are two writers and no way to tell
// which value a reader after the loop is seeing. The warning is correct here
// and must stay.
//
// It is in the corpus because the first attempt at ERROR-ZYB-003 removed the
// false warning by removing the mark altogether — silencing this one too. The
// analyzer's own unit test caught it, and a case that only lives in a unit test
// is a case the other two engines are not held to.
@ i:1..3 {
    >> i ¶
    i = i + 1
}
